{"filePath": ".tmp-rel22.json", "content": "{
  "tag_name": "v1.10.22-qa",
  "name": "IVX Holdings v1.10.22 — Owner sign-in: 3 real defects found and fixed",
  "draft": false,
  "prerelease": false,
  "body": "## The black screen is gone. This is a different, real defect.\n\nv1.10.21 fixed the routing black screen — the login screen renders. Sign-in then failed with **\"Login service temporarily unavailable. Please try again.\"**\n\nThat message is **not** an outage. Live probe of the production backend during this fix:\n\n```\nPOST https://api.ivxholding.com/api/members/login   HTTP 401   0.32s\nGET  https://api.ivxholding.com/health              HTTP 200   1.11s\n```\n\nThe backend was up the whole time. That string is a hardcoded **6-second gateway timeout fallback** inside the app's own backend.\n\n## Defect 1 — deadline inversion (backend/hono.ts)\n\nThe login route was wrapped in a generic 6s deadline:\n\n```ts\nwithTimeout(() => handleMemberLogin(...), () => 503 'Login service temporarily unavailable')\nconst SB_HARD_TIMEOUT_MS = 6_000;\n```\n\nBut the handler's own Supabase sign-in budget was **10 seconds**.\n\n**The outer deadline was shorter than the inner one.** Any sign-in needing 6-10s could *never* succeed — the wrapper answered 503 before the sign-in could return. Correct password, guaranteed failure. Nothing was logged as an error, because the inner call was still running normally when the response had already been sent.\n\nFixed: login now has its own `LOGIN_HARD_TIMEOUT_MS = 20s`, and the inner budget is `MEMBER_LOGIN_INNER_BUDGET_MS = 8s`. Outer exceeds inner by 12s of headroom.\n\n## Defect 2 — a bookkeeping write could fail a verified login\n\n```ts\nawait Promise.race([updateMemberLastLogin(userId), reject after 3s]);\n```\n\nThis ran **after** the password was verified and a session already existed. A slow `profiles` write threw, the outer catch swallowed it, and a **successful** login was returned to the app as **HTTP 401 with a raw internal message**.\n\nFixed: it is now fire-and-forget. A non-critical write can never fail an authenticated login.\n\n## Defect 3 — the client lied about every failure\n\n```ts\nreturn { failureReason: 'service_unavailable', supabaseErrorStatus: 504 };\n```\n\nEvery non-success response was reported as `service_unavailable` with a hardcoded 504 — **including a plain HTTP 401 wrong password**, a 429 rate limit, and a 403 unconfirmed email.\n\nThis is the reason the defect survived so many builds: the error message carried **zero diagnostic signal**. Wrong password and server outage looked identical on screen.\n\nFixed — classification by real HTTP status:\n\n- `401` → Invalid email or password\n- `403` → Verification required\n- `429` → Rate limited\n- `5xx` / transport failure → Service unavailable (the only path that may claim this)\n- real status code preserved instead of a fabricated 504\n\nPlus: a retryable 5xx/transport failure is now **retried once with 1.2s backoff**, and a definitive answer (wrong password, rate limit) is **not** replayed against fallback URLs where it would burn the rate-limit budget.\n\n## Permanent guards — 21 new tests\n\n`__tests__/owner-login-timeout-invariant.test.ts` fails the build if any of the three returns:\n\n- **INVARIANT: outer route deadline > inner budget** — the exact inversion that caused this\n- outer must keep >= 5s headroom over inner\n- `updateMemberLastLogin` must stay fire-and-forget and must never be awaited in a throwing race\n- 401/403/429/5xx each map to the correct reason (7 table-driven status cases)\n- the hardcoded `supabaseErrorStatus: 504` must not come back\n\n## Validation\n\n- `runChecks` (TypeScript + lint + structure): **0 errors**\n- New login tests: **21 pass / 0 fail**\n- Combined login + routing guards: **28 pass / 0 fail**\n- Full suite: **1164 pass**, 3 pre-existing unrelated failures\n- Gradle: **BUILD SUCCESSFUL**\n\nVerified in the shipped bundle: `invalid_credentials`, `rate_limited`, `verification_required`, retry logging, `Login failed:` structured log, build stamp `1.10.22 (120)`, and all four v1.10.21 defence layers retained.\n\nversionName 1.10.22 / versionCode 120\nSHA256: `4126e19b5f18d6b10bdd77213af0393c6eaea5ee54de445ff9cdb1cfa5477697`\n\n> Note: defects 1 and 2 are backend changes. They take effect when the Render backend redeploys from this commit. Defect 3 (honest error classification + retry) is in this APK and takes effect immediately — after installing, a wrong password says *wrong password*, and a real outage says *outage*."
}
